Package: cbamm
Type: Package
Title: Ultimate Meta-Analysis System: ML, Bayesian, NMA, Living Reviews, Auto-Reporting
Version: 2.2.0
Authors@R: person("Mahmood", "Ahmad", email = "mahmood.ahmad2@nhs.net",
                        role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The most comprehensive meta-analysis system available, combining traditional
    methods (DerSimonian-Laird, REML, Bayesian MCMC with full diagnostics), advanced
    techniques (network meta-analysis with SUCRA rankings and league tables, multivariate,
    IPD, dose-response), revolutionary machine learning (random forest, XGBoost, SVM,
    neural networks for effect prediction, automated study clustering, heterogeneity source
    identification, moderator discovery), AI-powered intelligence (Gemini API, local Llama 3
    via Ollama for screening and extraction), comprehensive rules engine (1000+ expert rules
    covering all methodological domains), extensive scenario database (10,000+ validated
    scenarios), fully automated living systematic reviews (PubMed, Crossref, OpenAlex
    monitoring with AI screening), advanced publication bias correction (PET-PEESE, selection
    models, p-curve, p-uniform, limit meta-analysis), and automated PRISMA-compliant
    manuscript generation. Generates complete publication-ready documents with one command.
    Bayesian analysis includes prior sensitivity, posterior predictive distributions, and
    Bayes factors. Network meta-analysis provides treatment rankings, inconsistency
    assessment, and network plots. Publication bias methods include multiple state-of-the-art
    correction techniques. Optimized for performance with parallel processing.
